        "id": 77249,
        "name": "Envisioner",
        "username": "Envisioner",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-10-15T05:12:51.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Thanks for finding that.&nbsp; I was indeed fighting the Matriarch, so the probability of getting most of her deck into her trash and then stacking her deck with all the Darken the Skies at the top and the Mask at the bottom is very realistic.&nbsp; Fortunately, it didn't matter, as Visi had other cards she could play, and the heroes slaughtered the unlucky Lilian (who had just randomly <em>drawn</em> all her Darkens at the start of the game, only ever getting four Fowl out and one of those was Timeshifted into play by Omnitronks, just so the heroes could kill it).&nbsp; Still, it's annoying that rulings like this are hard to find in a hurry, as I never ever think of them until the situation appears in play (and strongly dislike the \"just do whatever you feel like doing\" approach).</p><p>Also that's a hilarious alternate definition of \"conservatives and liberals\".</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:58:11.994Z",
