        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"dpt\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dpt/48/1922_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> dpt:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>dypaca wrote:</b><br><blockquote>Actually there is at least one card which seems to assume an order to the trash.&nbsp; Silver Gultch's 'Lost in the Past' puts the top card of the environment&nbsp;trash on the bottom of the environment deck.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nThank you. With two cards that at least appear to depend on the order of the trash, I'm now inclined to think you should keep the trash in order.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>You would think that the cards that state explicitly that order should matter would&nbsp;be viewed as&nbsp;exceptions to the general rule instead of a confirmation of them&nbsp;(after all, isn't that the purpose of card text in the first place? To provide instructions to the player&nbsp;that are&nbsp;outside of the general game system?)</p>",
        "post_number": 8,
        "post_type": 1,
