        "raw": "[quote=\"dpt\"]\n\n&nbsp;\n<div class=\"bb-quote\"><b>dypaca wrote:</b><br /><blockquote class=\"bb-quote-body\">Actually there is at least one card which seems to assume an order to the trash.&nbsp; Silver Gultch&#39;s &#39;Lost in the Past&#39; puts the top card of the environment&nbsp;trash on the bottom of the environment deck.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nThank you. With two cards that at least appear to depend on the order of the trash, I&#39;m now inclined to think you should keep the trash in order.\n\n[/quote]\n\nYou would think that the cards that state explicitly that order should matter would&nbsp;be viewed as&nbsp;exceptions to the general rule instead of a confirmation of them&nbsp;(after all, isn&#39;t that the purpose of card text in the first place? To provide instructions to the player&nbsp;that are&nbsp;outside of the general game system?)\n",
